  "details": "The matcap function for the toon standard looks off when put next to any point lights, at first I didn't quite understand why but I believe that what's happening is the lighting from realtime non-directional lights is getting overlayed on top of the matcap rather than the matcap getting overlayed onto the lit up model. This ends up with the matcap looking bad in various instances, and just being a bit inconsistent.\n\nI've put more information in a reply below that I have tested since then",
